and binary-package exception are in licenses/pcre2/license.md; SLJIT's
BSD-2-Clause terms are in the source copyright notices. Unicode 16 data
attribution and Unicode License V3 are in licenses/unicode/.

Every locked third-party Cargo package, including runtime, compiler,
build-time, proc-macro, and platform-specific dependencies, is listed with
its exact version, published archive checksum, license selection, source,
and bundled upstream license/copyright files in licenses/cargo/inventory.json.
Dual-licensed crates are used under Apache-2.0 where available, otherwise
MIT; unicode-ident additionally requires Unicode-3.0. r-efi uses its
Apache-2.0 option, not the alternative LGPL option. The wrapper pcre2-sys
uses MIT; its bundled PCRE2/SLJIT sources retain their separate licenses.

The actual build toolchain's Rust standard-library attribution and complete
license texts are in licenses/rust/. Rust's in-tree and third-party notices
are preserved verbatim in licenses/rust/copyright.html; its compiler version
and file hashes are in licenses/rust/inventory.json. The Rust compiler itself
is not redistributed. System libraries and the external clang/LLVM and
Mix/Elixir build tools are not bundled as Tonic executables.

Distribute license, notice, and licenses/ alongside the Tonic compiler and
